 An Admission Of Truth

I pleaded— pleaded— pleaded;
And you would not hear:
I tried— I tried— I tried;
And you were deaf as any crowd;
You would not listen— you turned away;
You treated me curtly, coldly,
As mere acquaintance unknown.

I lingered— lingered— lingered;
You gave me no smile;
I talked—

